 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 640397,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/02733dcb5599a9ee.jpg\" alt=\"The table has two columns, date and N. The date 5/1/12 corresponds with N 56, 6/1/12 with 98, 7/2/12 with 203, and 8/10/12 with 421.\"></p>\n\n<p>These data were collected on a population of beetles in Florida. \nBased on the data, how would you describe population growth in this case and what do you predict about growth of this population in the future? Explain your reasoning.</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1249077,
     "content_html": "Population shows logistic growth, as number of individuals doubles every month and will likely continue to grow logistically until its resources become depleted. At that point, the population growth rate will slow down and level off to zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 1249078,
     "content_html": "The population shows exponential growth, as the number of individuals doubles every month and will likely grow logistically in the future when the resources become limited. At that point, the population growth rate will slow down and level off to zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 1249080,
     "content_html": "The population shows exponential growth, as number of individuals doubles every month and will likely continue to grow exponentially until its resources become limited. At that point, the growth will become logistic; the population growth rate will slow down and level off to zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 1249079,
     "content_html": "The population shows logistic growth and is likely to grow exponentially as the resources are probably increasing. The population growth rate will increase in the future as well."
    }
   ],
